          "name": "Code Quality Analyzer",
          "rules": [
            {
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A broad exception handler can hide failures it cannot recover from."
              },
              "help": {
                "markdown": "**Broad exception handler** (`PY-COR-002`)\n\nA broad exception handler can hide failures it cannot recover from.\n\n**Remediation:** Catch the narrow exception types the operation can recover from.\n\n**Not reported when:**\n\n- The handler catches a specific exception class rather than Exception or BaseException.\n- The handler body is only `pass`/`...` (a bare `except:`, `except Exception: pass`, ...): PY-COR-003 reports the swallow and one handler yields one finding, not two.\n- The handler ends with a bare `raise` or `raise <bound name>` (no `from`): `except BaseException: cleanup(); raise` is a `finally` with access to the exception and the only way to guarantee cleanup on KeyboardInterrupt; ruff BLE001 exempts the same shape. Logging without re-raising, or wrapping in a new exception type, is still reported.\n\n[PY-COR-002 in the rule reference](https://github.com/AmitSinghOM/code-quality-analyzer/blob/v3.5.0/docs/RULES.md#py-cor-002-broad-exception-handler)",
                "text": "Catch the narrow exception types the operation can recover from."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/AmitSinghOM/code-quality-analyzer/blob/v3.5.0/docs/RULES.md#py-cor-002-broad-exception-handler",
              "id": "PY-COR-002",
              "name": "broad-exception-handler",
              "properties": {
                "category": "correctness",
                "confidence": "high",
                "defaultSeverity": "warning",
                "language": "python"
              },
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Broad exception handler"
              }
            },
            {
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A value bound to a secret-shaped name (token, password, nonce, salt, otp, api_key, session id, csrf) is produced by the random module."
              },
              "help": {
                "markdown": "**Non-cryptographic random used for a secret** (`PY-SEC-005`)\n\nA value bound to a secret-shaped name (token, password, nonce, salt, otp, api_key, session id, csrf) is produced by the random module.\n\n**CWE:** CWE-330\n\n**Remediation:** Generate secrets with the secrets module (token_urlsafe, choice).\n\n**Not reported when:**\n\n- The bound name or keyword does not match the secret-shaped pattern (languages/_security.is_secret_name); `counter = random.randint(...)` is fine.\n- The expression mentions SystemRandom, or uses the secrets module.\n\n[PY-SEC-005 in the rule reference](https://github.com/AmitSinghOM/code-quality-analyzer/blob/v3.5.0/docs/RULES.md#py-sec-005-non-cryptographic-random-used-for-a-secret)",
                "text": "Generate secrets with the secrets module (token_urlsafe, choice)."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/AmitSinghOM/code-quality-analyzer/blob/v3.5.0/docs/RULES.md#py-sec-005-non-cryptographic-random-used-for-a-secret",
              "id": "PY-SEC-005",
              "name": "insecure-random-for-secret",
              "properties": {
                "category": "security",
                "confidence": "medium",
                "defaultSeverity": "warning",
                "language": "python",
                "security-severity": "5.9",
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "external/cwe/cwe-330"
                ]
              },
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Non-cryptographic random used for a secret"
              }
            }
          ],
          "semanticVersion": "3.5.0"
        }
      }
